2. APNIC delegated statistics (geoip/cn.txt)
   https://ftp.apnic.net/stats/apnic/delegated-apnic-latest
   The mainland China IPv4 and IPv6 ranges are computed from the records of country code
   CN with status allocated or assigned. The data is used under the APNIC conditions of
   use (https://www.apnic.net/about-apnic/legal/): it may be downloaded and used freely,
   and APNIC gives no warranty. The file is a registry of address delegations, not a map
   of physical locations, so it can differ from commercial GeoIP databases.

3. Telegram (geoip/telegram.txt)
   https://core.telegram.org/resources/cidr.txt
   The address ranges Telegram publishes for its own servers, used unchanged apart from
   sorting and merging adjacent ranges.

4. Google (geoip/google.txt)
   https://www.gstatic.com/ipranges/goog.json minus https://www.gstatic.com/ipranges/cloud.json
   Google documents this subtraction as the way to get the addresses of Google services
   (as opposed to Google Cloud customers). The files are published by Google for this
   purpose (https://support.google.com/a/answer/10026322).

5. Special-purpose addresses (geoip/private.txt)
   A fixed list written for this project from the IANA IPv4 and IPv6 Special-Purpose
   Address Registries (RFC 6890): 0.0.0.0/8, 10.0.0.0/8, 100.64.0.0/10, 127.0.0.0/8,
   169.254.0.0/16, 172.16.0.0/12, 192.0.0.0/24, 192.0.2.0/24, 192.88.99.0/24,
   192.168.0.0/16, 198.18.0.0/15, 198.51.100.0/24, 203.0.113.0/24, 224.0.0.0/3,
   ::/127, fc00::/7, fe80::/10, ff00::/8.

